---
// src/pages/about.astro
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const SKILLS = [
  'Writing and editing',
  'Research',
  'Fact-checking',
  'Event organizing',
  'Fundraising',
  'Volunteer coordination',
  'Social media',
  'Website and technology',
  'Data support',
  'Local outreach',
];
---
{/* The candidate portrait is set explicitly here. It used to be the site-wide
    default, which meant every page previewed as a campaign. This is the one
    page where the portrait is the correct share image. Jimmy is still the
    person behind this work, even though the page below it no longer reads
    as a campaign platform. */}
<Base
  title='About Jimmy Skovgard | The Wyoming Opposition'
  description='Jimmy Skovgard accepts the 2026 primary result. Here is why Skovgard2026.org continues as the Wyoming Opposition, and how to help hold Chuck Gray and Harriet Hageman accountable before November.'
  ogImage='/images/og-default.jpg'
  ogImageAlt='Jimmy Skovgard'
  ogImageWidth={1200}
  ogImageHeight={630}
>
  <Nav />
  <main class='pt-20'>

    <!-- Hero banner -->
    <div class='bg-wy-charcoal py-20 px-4'>
      <div class='max-w-5xl mx-auto grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center'>
        <div>
          <p class='text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-3'>The Wyoming Opposition</p>
          <h1 class='text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-bone mb-6 leading-tight'>About Jimmy Skovgard</h1>
          <p class='text-wy-bone/75 text-lg leading-relaxed'>
            Fifth-generation immigrant. Fourth-generation Wyomingite. Husband, father, veteran, and the neighbor
            behind the Wyoming Opposition, the citizen effort that continues the work this campaign started.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class='rounded-sm overflow-hidden shadow-2xl'>
          <img src='/images/jimmy.png' alt='Jimmy Skovgard' class='w-full object-cover' />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The primary is over -->
    <section class='bg-white py-16 px-4'>
      <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto'>
        <p class='text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sm mb-3'>Where Things Stand</p>
        <h2 class='text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-6'>The Primary Is Over. The Work Is Not.</h2>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4'>
          On August 18, 2026, Wyoming Republicans chose Harriet Hageman and Chuck Gray as their nominees. I accept
          that result. It was decided fair and square, and I am not going to pretend otherwise. This is not a
          campaign that is quietly still running.
        </p>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed'>
          But winning a nomination is not the finish line for accountability. Every one of us still has a say in
          whether the people we send to Washington answer for what they do there, and that responsibility did not
          start with my campaign and does not end with it either.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Who I am -->
    <section class='bg-wy-bone py-16 px-4'>
      <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto'>
        <p class='text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sm mb-3'>Who I Am</p>
        <h2 class='text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-6'>A Neighbor, Not a Career Politician</h2>
        <div class='prose prose-lg prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-wy-charcoal prose-a:text-wy-ember max-w-none'>
          <p>
            I grew up in the Big Horn Basin: grade school in Greybull, high school in Basin, and college at the
            University of Wyoming. My great-grandfather, Simon Skovgard, homesteaded near Basin in 1909. Like many
            of us, I was raised to work hard, speak the truth, and take responsibility for my actions.
          </p>
          <p>
            I served 12 years in the Wyoming Army National Guard and was honorably discharged as a captain. I have
            worked in the private sector, run my own business, and spent my life grounded in Wyoming values.
          </p>
          <p class='font-semibold text-wy-charcoal'>I never planned to run for office.</p>
          <p>
            I got off the couch in 2024 because the path of division, distraction, and fearmongering is wrong. Fear
            can sharpen the mind in a crisis, but right now it is being used to keep us angry and apart. Nothing is
            being built.
          </p>
          <p>
            I have seen this in my own family. A brother who forwards link after link filled with half-truths. A
            sister who lives in the Big Horn Basin and worries that &ldquo;illegals&rdquo; will invade her home.
            These are not natural divisions. This is deliberate manipulation for control, and it cuts deep.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why this continues -->
    <section class='bg-white py-16 px-4'>
      <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto'>
        <p class='text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sm mb-3'>Why This Continues</p>
        <h2 class='text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-6'>Going Quiet Was the Easy Way Out</h2>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4'>
          Shutting this website down and going quiet would have been the easy thing to do. It would also have
          thrown away every question we started asking, every piece of the record we started gathering, and every
          Wyoming neighbor who signed up because they wanted to be part of holding power accountable.
        </p>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed'>
          I am not willing to walk away from that. So the site keeps going, and the work keeps going with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What the Wyoming Opposition is -->
    <section class='bg-white border-y border-wy-dust py-20 px-4'>
      <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto'>
        <p class='text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sm mb-3'>What The Wyoming Opposition Is</p>
        <h2 class='text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-6'>An Unwatched Office Drifts</h2>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4'>
          Skovgard2026.org is now home to the Wyoming Opposition, a citizen effort that examines the public
          records of the people asking to represent us, publishes what it finds with sources attached, and asks
          the questions insiders would rather skip.
        </p>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4'>
          The Wyoming Opposition opposes both Harriet Hageman, running for U.S. Senate, and Chuck Gray, running
          for U.S. House and currently serving as Wyoming secretary of state. Our immediate objective this
          November is straightforward: inform and organize Wyoming voters, and keep Chuck Gray from winning that
          seat. Hageman's record stays under the same scrutiny.
        </p>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8'>
          This is not opposition for its own sake. Someone reading the record, asking the hard question in public,
          and writing down the answer is ordinary maintenance work in a republic. That work is easier together
          than alone, and it deserves more than one campaign's worth of attention.
        </p>
        <div class='flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4'>
          <a href='/the-record/chuck-gray' class='border-2 border-wy-charcoal text-wy-charcoal font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-sm tracking-wide hover:bg-wy-charcoal hover:text-wy-bone transition-colors text-center'>
            Read the record on Chuck Gray
          </a>
          <a href='/the-record/harriet-hageman' class='border-2 border-wy-charcoal text-wy-charcoal font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-sm tracking-wide hover:bg-wy-charcoal hover:text-wy-bone transition-colors text-center'>
            Read the record on Harriet Hageman
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Standards -->
    <section class='bg-wy-bone py-16 px-4'>
      <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto'>
        <p class='text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sm mb-3'>Standards and Corrections</p>
        <h2 class='text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-6'>We Are Not Asking You to Take Our Word for It</h2>
        <div class='space-y-4 mb-6'>
          {[
            'Every factual claim about a public official’s record links to an original or authoritative source.',
            'Opinion and judgment are clearly labeled as opinion or judgment, not presented as fact.',
            'The record is corrected when new evidence emerges, or when something in it is wrong.',
          ].map(item => (
            <div class='flex gap-4 items-start bg-white border border-wy-dust rounded-sm p-5'>
              <span class='text-wy-ember text-xl mt-0.5' aria-hidden='true'>&#10003;</span>
              <p class='text-wy-charcoal/85'>{item}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed font-semibold'>
          We are not asking anyone to take our word for it. We are asking Wyoming people to examine the record.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What guides this work -->
    <section class='bg-wy-charcoal py-20 px-4'>
      <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto'>
        <h2 class='text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-bone mb-4 text-center'>What Guides This Work</h2>
        <p class='text-wy-bone/70 text-lg mb-10 text-center'>A short list of principles, not a platform.</p>
        <div class='space-y-4 text-left'>
          {[
            'Public office belongs to the people who are governed by it.',
            'The Constitution and the rule of law apply to everyone, including the people who hold office.',
            'Wyoming voices should guide Wyoming choices, not distant money or national factions.',
            'Facts come before party loyalty.',
            'Winning an election is not immunity from accountability.',
          ].map(principle => (
            <div class='flex gap-4 items-start bg-white/10 rounded-sm p-5'>
              <span class='text-wy-sandstone text-xl mt-0.5' aria-hidden='true'>&#10003;</span>
              <p class='text-wy-bone/90'>{principle}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class='mt-10 bg-white/10 border-l-4 border-wy-sandstone rounded-sm p-6'>
          <h3 class='font-serif font-bold text-wy-bone text-xl mb-2'>One Thing I Still Believe</h3>
          <p class='text-wy-bone/80 leading-relaxed mb-3'>
            On questions of life, family, and medical care, I still start with Wyoming&rsquo;s Constitution.
            Government should not force personal medical decisions on families.
          </p>
          <blockquote class='border-l-2 border-wy-sandstone/60 pl-4 italic text-wy-bone/70 mb-2'>
            &ldquo;Every competent adult has the right to make personal health care decisions for themselves and
            their dependents, and the State of Wyoming must protect those rights from undue governmental
            infringement.&rdquo;
          </blockquote>
          <p class='text-sm text-wy-bone/50'>Wyoming Constitution, Article 1, Section 38</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Your ballot in November -->
    <section class='bg-white py-16 px-4'>
      <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto'>
        <p class='text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sm mb-3'>Your Ballot in November</p>
        <h2 class='text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-6'>You Are Not Required to Give Away Your Vote</h2>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4'>
          If Chuck Gray has not earned your vote, you are not required to give it to him. Wyoming voters have two
          lawful choices in the U.S. House contest:
        </p>
        <ol class='space-y-4 mb-6'>
          <li class='bg-wy-bone border border-wy-dust rounded-sm p-5'>
            <p class='font-semibold text-wy-charcoal mb-1'>1. Vote for another qualified candidate.</p>
            <p class='text-wy-charcoal/75 text-sm leading-relaxed'>
              This both withholds a vote from Chuck Gray and adds a vote for someone else on the ballot.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class='bg-wy-bone border border-wy-dust rounded-sm p-5'>
            <p class='font-semibold text-wy-charcoal mb-1'>2. Complete the rest of your ballot and leave the U.S. House contest blank.</p>
            <p class='text-wy-charcoal/75 text-sm leading-relaxed'>
              An intentional undervote withholds support from Chuck Gray without adding a vote for anyone else.
              It is a deliberate choice, not a reason to skip the rest of the ballot.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed'>
          Investigate the choices in front of you and vote according to your own conscience. Check with your
          county clerk or Wyoming&rsquo;s official election website to confirm exactly who and what will be on
          your ballot before you vote.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Help build the opposition -->
    <section class='bg-wy-bone py-20 px-4 text-center'>
      <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto'>
        <p class='text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sm mb-3'>Help Build the Opposition</p>
        <h2 class='text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-4'>The Wyoming Opposition Is Just Getting Started</h2>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-10 max-w-xl mx-auto'>
          Join the Pulse to stay informed with no commitment beyond reading. If you are ready to help build this,
          tell us what you can do.
        </p>

        <div class='flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center mb-10'>
          <a href='/pulse' class='bg-wy-ember text-wy-bone font-bold px-8 py-4 rounded-sm text-lg tracking-wide hover:bg-wy-ember-dark transition-colors shadow-sm text-center'>
            Join the Pulse
          </a>
          <a href='/volunteer' class='border-2 border-wy-charcoal text-wy-charcoal font-bold px-8 py-4 rounded-sm text-lg tracking-wide hover:bg-wy-charcoal hover:text-wy-bone transition-colors text-center'>
            Volunteer Your Skills
          </a>
        </div>

        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/60 text-sm mb-4'>We can use help with:</p>
        <div class='flex flex-wrap gap-2 justify-center mb-10'>
          {SKILLS.map(skill => (
            <span class='bg-white border border-wy-dust rounded-sm px-3 py-1 text-sm text-wy-charcoal/80'>{skill}</span>
          ))}
        </div>

        <p class='text-wy-charcoal/80 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-xl mx-auto mb-2'>
          Together we can document the record, organize our voices, and keep Chuck Gray from winning in November.
        </p>
        <p class='text-wy-charcoal font-serif font-bold text-2xl'>Public office belongs to us. Let&rsquo;s act like it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Substack CTA -->
    <section class='bg-white border-t border-wy-dust py-16 px-4 text-center'>
      <h2 class='text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-4'>Dig Deeper</h2>
      <p class='text-wy-charcoal/70 text-lg mb-8 max-w-xl mx-auto'>
        Hundreds of essays on Jimmy&rsquo;s journey and the path forward. Read the Substack, then join the
        conversation on the podcast.
      </p>
      <div class='flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center'>
        <a href='https://jimskovgard.substack.com/' target='_blank' rel='noopener'
           class='bg-wy-charcoal text-wy-bone font-bold px-8 py-3 rounded-sm hover:bg-wy-charcoal/85 transition-colors'>
          Read on Substack
        </a>
        <a href='/podcast' class='border-2 border-wy-charcoal text-wy-charcoal font-bold px-8 py-3 rounded-sm hover:bg-wy-charcoal hover:text-wy-bone transition-colors'>
          Listen to Podcast
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
